  "narrative": "The mandatory precondition passed. resolve_replay_plan({\"game\":\"bp35\",\"levels_reproduced\":6}, Path(\".\")) selected results/outer_loop_codex55_bp35_probe_round10_20260712.json, returned 225 labels, and a fresh reset replay reached frame_level=6 with state=NOT_FINISHED. That first mapping process consumed 225 env.step calls. A second fresh environment replayed the same 225-label prefix, then used one ACTION5 no-op as an early timer control: position, gravity, and objects were unchanged while the action timer/HUD advanced. Inspection of the executable level-specific timer branch established that L7-L9 use a 128-action per-level budget, double L6's 64; the death boundary was not intentionally burned because the exact branch and live increment were already grounded and preserving calls allowed a fresh reproduction gate. The solved L7 route used 44 actions including that control no-op. From (3,19), three RIGHT moves reached (6,19); solidifying the open X at (6,21) and reversing gravity created a perch at (6,20). RIGHT, reverse gravity, RIGHT entered the mid-right shaft at (8,15). Two LEFT moves, a reversal, and two more LEFT moves reached the upper edge of the central X field. Solidifying (4,14), reversing, and moving LEFT twice dropped safely to (2,8). The lower zig-zag then used shields (4,9), (5,10), and (6,9) as alternating doors and landing supports to cross the paired pillar columns and arrive at (7,4). Solidifying (7,7), reversing gravity, then moving RIGHT twice reached (9,26) through the safe column-9 express shaft. Two LEFT moves, a reversal to (7,23), four LEFT moves to (3,23), and one final gravity-switch click landed on the goal at (3,25), advancing frame_level from 6 to 7 and loading L8 alive. The live winning run consumed 269 calls including the prefix. A third fresh environment replayed all 269 saved labels through arc_solver_kit.reproduce(claimed_level=7) and returned reached_level=7, reproduced=true. Total usage was 225+269+269=763 env.step calls.",
